// HealthReorientation How much a turn re-read before it worked, counted from the Read and Edit tool calls the turn reported. Absent where the turn was summarised before this was collected (finished turns are not re-summarised, so those stay without it). On a total it is the sum over the turns that have it; `turns` says how many those are, which can be fewer than the total's `turns`. A read or edit that failed is not counted. Reads with no reported path (outside the workspace, or a sensitive name) are counted in `reads` but never as repeats. Compactions are not here: the harness does not report them yet.
type HealthReorientation struct {
	// EditedTurns Turns counted here that made at least one edit; 0 or 1 on a turn.
	EditedTurns int `json:"edited_turns"`

	// Edits Edit and Write calls.
	Edits int `json:"edits"`

	// Reads Read calls.
	Reads int `json:"reads"`

	// ReadsBeforeFirstEdit Read calls before the first edit; null when the turn made no edit. On a total it is the sum over the edited turns, so divide by `edited_turns` for an average.
	ReadsBeforeFirstEdit *int `json:"reads_before_first_edit"`

	// RereadCalls Read calls of a path the same turn had already read. The harness reports no range, so reading one large file in pages counts as repeats.
	RereadCalls int `json:"reread_calls"`

	// RereadsFromEarlierTurns Paths this turn read that an earlier turn in the same native context (the same kagent session) had read or edited. A Mainloop session that moves to a new kagent session starts a new context, and its earlier turns do not count.
	RereadsFromEarlierTurns int `json:"rereads_from_earlier_turns"`

	// Turns Turns counted here; 1 on a turn.
	Turns int `json:"turns"`
}

